course: dictionary
lesson: 4075
title: Context clues: germ
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A germ is a very tiny living thing, too small to see, that can make people or animals ill. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Vultures eat dead animals before their germs can spread.» Spread is the clue: germs travel from one place to another and can make things ill.
explain: «Washing hands with soap for about 20 seconds removes most germs.» Removes is a clue. If you take something away, it is no longer there, so washing takes germs off your hands. «Their strong stomach acid kills germs that would make other animals ill.» Kills and ill are clues that germs can make bodies unwell.
explain: Germ has other meanings too. In «the germ of an idea», germ means the very beginning of something that grows. Germ is also the part of a seed that grows into a plant. Read the whole sentence to find out which meaning the writer means.
fact: A germ is a very tiny living thing, too small to see, that can make people or animals ill.
fact: Germs include bacteria, viruses and fungi; most bacteria are harmless or helpful.
fact: Germs spread through coughs, sneezes, dirty hands and food.
fact: Washing hands with soap for 20 seconds removes most germs; covering a cough and not sharing drinks when ill also help.
fact: The germ of an idea means the very beginning of something that grows.
exercise: What is a germ? | *A very tiny living thing, too small to see, that can make people ill | A huge animal that lives in the sea | A kind of bread roll | A type of cloud
exercise: «Their strong stomach acid kills germs that would make other animals ill.» What does kills mean here? | Makes them grow bigger | Hides them under the skin | Carries them to new places | *Destroys them, so they die
exercise: Which of these is a good way to stop germs spreading? | Leave dirty hands unwashed | *Cover your mouth when you cough | Share your drink with a friend when you are ill | Lick your fingers after eating
test: Why does breath smell in the morning, according to «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow in the mouth overnight»? | *Because germs grow in the mouth overnight when there is less spit | Because you are tired | Because the sun is up | Because you ate too much sugar
test: «Her idea was just the germ of a bigger plan.» What does germ mean here? | A loud noise | A tiny animal that can make you ill | *The very beginning of something that grows | A kind of cloud
exam: Why is washing hands with soap for about 20 seconds useful? | *It removes most germs | It makes hands smell nice | It stops you feeling hungry | It makes your skin grow
